WEBVTT

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.717
At the beginning of that summer, I went to live with
my grandmother in this town in the countryside.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.074
We'll return as soon as your grandmother gets well.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.078
Yeah.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.959
Really, it's a shame you have to change schools at such an important time like this.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.678
I'll be fine, really.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.479
If she heard you say that, Shuuhei-san, your grandmother
wouldn't have to worry anymore either.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.194
Oh, that's right!

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.399
They just finished tuning the piano in the lesson room yesterday.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:10.909
Then I can start today?

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.549
Yes, we can start your lessons!

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:14.638
Yeah.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.671
You simply must become a fabulous pianist just like your father.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.077
It's a forest.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.475
You're right! It's a big forest, isn't it?

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:44.677
A piano?

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.313
What's wrong, Shuuhei-san?

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.597
Did you hear a piano just now?

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:54.116
A piano?

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.595
| didn't hear anything.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:57.317
| see.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:00.989
Was it just my imagination?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:03:00.479
The Piano Forest
Piano no Mori

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.114
Today, I'd like to introduce you all to a new friend.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.192
Amamiya Shuuhei-kun.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.316
Now, Amamiya-kun, will you introduce yourself for us?

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:16.112
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.355
I'm Amamiya Shuuhei and I came here from Tokyo.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.876
My special skill is that I've been learning to play the piano since I was four years old.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.120
My dream is to become a pianist.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.230
Everyone! Quiet down!

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.229
Plays the piano he said, even though he's a guy.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:38.112
That's right.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.116
A transfer student shouldn't stand out.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.151
If he stands out...

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.837
Amamiya Shuuhei-kun.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.031
What is it?

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.511
Do you know about the piano in the forest?

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.394
Piano in the forest?

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.279
You know there's a huge forest near the school, don't you?

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.916
Oh, that forest.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.790
There's been a broken piano in that forest for a long time.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.870
Of course, since it's broken, you can't get any sound out of it.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.031
However, when night falls, for some reason that piano...

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:21.394
Tum! Tum! All on its own, the piano goes tum, tum!

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:25.237
The dead body of a man was found nearby.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:31.157
Rumor says his spirit appears night after night and plays that piano.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:35.599
Amamiya-kun, there's a challenge to test your courage.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.638
Go into the forest and play it — the ghost piano.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.594
Huh? Th-That's impossible.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.630
| can't play a broken piano.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:50.031
Of course you can play it! After all, you've been learning
the piano since you were four years old.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:55.040
Yeah, this is what happens to you when you stand out.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:57.677
Understand, this is an initiation.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:01.795
An initiation to prove whether you're really a man or not.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.875
Either you go and play the ghost piano in the forest...

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.277
Or else you'll have to show us your penis.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:08.789
It's gotta be one or the other.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.794
There it is. Kinpira's "Show me your penis."

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.438
This is just a simple test of courage. You can't refuse.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:19.273
Even if it doesn't make a sound, you can still say that you played it.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.079
It won't make a sound anyway.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.150
Right, right!

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.596
It's a piano, so it produces sound.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:36.080
Amanmiya, don't worry. You can get sound from that piano.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.153
Stop making stuff up, Kai!

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.198
When I did my test of courage,
| couldn't get any sound out of it.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:47.952
Well, that's because you were shaking in your boots the entire time, Kinpira.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:50.349
You were too scared to play the piano.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:52.830
Maybe you should have to show it to everyone.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:57.240
Your itty bitty...

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:58.350
I'll kill you!

00:05:58.720 --> 00:05:59.471
...penis!

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.599
How dare you say that!

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.193
Ouch!

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.637
You lying bastard!

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.869
Damn you! Damn you! Damn you!

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:15.714
That piano...

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:16.755
...can't make a sound!

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.115
It's not a lie!

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.509
It's my piano, so I know for sure!

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:24.998
Your piano?!

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.478
Tell me, Kai.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:31.269
How can a poor family like yours afford to buy a piano?

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:38.030
Oh, I get it. You stole it. I forgot that your entire neighborhood is filled with thieves.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:41.511
Or maybe one of your mother's clients bought it for her?

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.718
Answer me, Kai!

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.277
Someone threw it out, so I took it.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.757
| will tell you something, Kinpira.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.913
| have lots of things you can't buy with money.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:54.799
For example: a giant penis!

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:02.999
Stop saying shit to make fun of me!

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.150
You should shut up yourself.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.671
Your breath reeks because your brains are all rotted!

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:09.795
You bastard!

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.190
Get him, get him! Do it!

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.796
What's going on? Finish cleaning up and go home.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:22.759
It's "Funeral” Ajino!

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:32.194
Do you have something to say?

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.076
What should I do?

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.793
| want to go home, but my legs aren't responding.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.599
If you don't, then head home.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.198
Uhm, is the legend about the piano in the forest really true?

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.711
The story about the piano in the forest is a lie.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:58.200
It was just made up. It's like one of those "Seven Wonders of the School".

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.234
I-| see. Goodbye.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.238
Ichinose
Kai

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.115
Hold it, Ichinose!

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:34.911
How many times do I have to tell you? If you get into one more fight...

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:35.318
| won't listen to what a liar has to say!
How many times do I have to tell you? If you get into one more fight...

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.038
| won't listen to what a liar has to say!

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:38.511
Liar?

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.560
Even though the piano in the forest is broken, it can still produce sound.

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:44.070
Because it's my piano!

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:45.949
Your piano?

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:50.638
Don't talk like you know everything! Especially when you're wrong.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.675
Amamiyal!

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.719
Uhm, you're Ichinose-kun, right?

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:19.791
Just call me Kai.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:25.196
Say, Amamiya, do you want to go now and see for yourself
that the piano in the forest can produce sound?

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:26.994
Huh? Now?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.434
Yeah. Come on!

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:30.194
H-Hold on.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:31.959
Wait up, Kai-kun!

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.717
You're slow, Amamiya!

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.231
You run slow, don't you?

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.833
Kai-kun, why did you save me back there?

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:52.397
Save you?

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.116
You know, when we were cleaning.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.831
You play the piano, don't you?

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.156
Yeah.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:04.877
| do too.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.396
You do too?

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.996
That's why I'm really glad now!

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:11.916
Let's go!

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:13.511
Wait a second!

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:21.353
| can't afford to injure my hands.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:23.516
| should be okay with these.

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:32.675
But, are we really going to be able to find the piano inside this huge forest?

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.799
We'll find it! I go there every day.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.392
Even with my eyes closed...

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:47.752
Amamiya, you must be my good luck charm.

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:51.433
Look! The piano's in a good mood today as well.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:05.832
I-It's a piano.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:11.311
This is the piano in the forest?

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:14.072
| can't believe it'd be here.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.837
It's so beautiful, like it's on a stage!

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:19.956
It's the first time I've ever seen anything like it.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:22.078
It's even more beautiful at night.

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:29.470
Okay, Kai-kun, I'm gonna play it.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:31.953
You can be my witness.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.880
So it really is broken. There's no sound.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:53.834
That's not true. It makes sound!

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:55.515
But, listen.

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:59.632
Try and play harder.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:04.471
Let me show you.

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:07.714
It's never not made a sound.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:10.480
Not even once.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.274
See?

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:18.273
Wh-Why?

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.799
Why did it make a sound?

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.596
How did you get it to produce sound?

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:25.679
Tell me, Kai-kun!

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:28.479
| don't know.

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:36.155
Since it's my piano, maybe it only opens up its heart for me.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:39.393
| suppose it must need some special style of playing.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.436
Kai-kun, will you play some piece of music for me?

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.752
Then maybe I can figure something out.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:49.913
Guess I have to.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:04.516
Kai-kun...

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.470
Amazing!

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.274
That was amazing, Kai-kun!

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:06.995
| don't know how else to say it but that was amazing!

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:10.153
D-Don't be silly! You're so dramatic.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.355
I'm serious!

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:15.594
Not only am I surprised that you can get sound out of it, but you can really play!

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:19.917
You're making me feel uncomfortable. That's
the first time I've played for another person.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:23.754
There's no reason to feel uncomfortable. You could
play for anyone without embarrassment.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.638
Hey, who are you taking lessons from?

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:30.038
Lessons? I've never taken lessons.

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:31.790
Not even once?

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:37.273
It's just like Kinpira said, my family is poor.

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:44.435
I'm not cut out for formal lessons anyway.

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:48.630
K-Kai-kun.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:49.996
If it's okay,

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:53.429
will you come and play my family's piano?

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:56.320
Huh? Your family's piano?

00:14:56.920 --> 00:15:01.198
Oh, I see! You have a piano inside your house!

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:04.838
It's in the lesson room. It's a grand piano too.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:08.435
Wow! You have a lesson room in your house?!

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:14.429
Amamiya, your piano is awesome!

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:16.034
Eeek! Kai-kun...

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:18.429
| can move my fingers incredibly quickly.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.270
It's like I'm under a spell.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:25.839
K-Kai-kun, you need to play softer, like you usually do.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:28.476
Huh? I always play this way.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.474
What the heck happened to Kai-kun?

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:38.718
Kai-kun, I get it. This time try playing a bit more slowly.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:40.355
Slowly?

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:45.958
Yes, that's it, Kai-kun! Just like that...

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:47.440
Don't let your mind drift.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.110
There you go. You can play just fine when you try.

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:56.633
This is kinda tiring and it's no fun.

00:15:56.880 --> 00:16:00.510
But Kai-kun, practice isn't supposed to be fun.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:03.356
But playing the piano is just for fun!

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:05.513
Don't you have fun when you play?

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:08.869
It's not just for fun.

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:13.390
If I can't handle the pain of practicing, I won't become a pianist.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:17.754
Okay, now try and play something that way.

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:24.839
Ajino is just like that too. He won't let us have any fun during music class.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:29.394
That's because Ajino-sensei isn't teaching music just for fun either.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:31.357
Ajino?

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:41.274
Hello. Shuuhei-san, is this your friend?

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:43.632
Yeah, Ichinose Kai-kun.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:44.916
Hello.

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:47.273
I'm Shuuhei's mother.

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:49.796
You play the piano too, Ichinose-kun?

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:52.680
Not really, I just play for fun.

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:54.990
It's too difficult to learn to play the piano properly.

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:56.799
Don't worry, Kai-kun.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.316
When you get used to practicing, you learn quickly.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:02.798
Say, did you say "Ajino-sensei" earlier?

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.798
Yeah, he's the music teacher.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:06.758
He's a very scary teacher though.

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:10.278
His name wouldn't be Ajino Sousuke, would it?

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.033
Yeah, that's it.

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:15.598
But we all secretly call him Ajino Soushiki (funeral).

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.269
Because his face always looks like he's at a funeral.

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:22.557
N-No way, it couldn't be...

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:24.395
Let me see.

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:25.677
Found it!

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:32.556
Is this him?

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:39.199
Oh, that's Ajino! He's really young, but it's Ajino.

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:42.552
Mother, do you know Ajino-sensei?

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:49.671
Oh, I know him all right! H-He was the pianist that all
of us music students at college aspired to be like.

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:52.151
Huh? A pianist?

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:58.199
Ajino Sousuke won the All-Japan competition while he was at college.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:02.434
And he had a spectacular debut as a pianist at the same time as he graduated college.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:07.191
Being able to accomplish all that was nothing short of a miracle.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:10.555
Did you know this, Kai-kun?

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:12.473
| had no idea.

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:14.956
This all happened over twenty years ago.

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:19.792
But I've never seen Ajino play the piano.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:24.598
He had an unfortunate accident five years after his professional debut.

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:29.993
He severely injured his left hand so he was forced to retire from being a pianist.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:34.232
| can't believe he'd be teaching elementary school music.

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:44.995
Are you seriously going to have Ajino-sensei be my piano tutor?

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:51.999
Of course I'm serious, Shuuhei-san! We're lucky to have
come out here and happened to find Ajino Sousuke!

00:18:58.520 --> 00:18:59.510
Sorry to disappoint you.

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:02.716
| don't think I'd be much help to him.

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:06.752
I'm no longer as I once was.

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:09.034
Please go now.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:13.356
| apologize for such a strange request.

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.149
Let's go, Mom.

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:20.273
Oh, Sensei...

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:26.036
The piano in the forest is broken but it can still make sound.

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:30.792
| thought we had discussed that once already.

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:32.878
But it's the truth.

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:36.039
Kai-kun is the only one who can make it play.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:37.397
Kai?

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:42.516
I'm telling the truth. I saw it with my own eyes and heard it with my own ears.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:48.434
I-1 tried my best to get sound out of it, but no matter what I did, it wouldn't come out.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.793
Even so, Kai-kun was somehow able to get it to play.

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:54.949
But what really surprised me was the tone of the piano.

00:19:55.320 --> 00:20:00.190
How can I put this, I've never heard a throbbing reverberation like that before.

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:05.193
You should be able to hear it as well.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:08.314
Because it looks like Kai-kun plays that piano every night.

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:10.677
Every night?

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:26.711
Kai, hurry and finish or you'll be grumbling when you have to do without dinner.

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:27.835
Yes, ma'am.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:32.678
Hey, Kai, what's Reiko doing?

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:33.829
Like I know!

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:41.118
What's with that kind of attitude in front of your customers?!

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:42.758
You're not my customer!

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:46.231
What?! If I'm Reiko's customer then that makes me your customer!

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:52.110
It looks like you don't understand your position here.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.756
Hey, stop that.

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:56.592
Rei-chan will be here soon.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:59.395
Shut your mouth! Stay out of this, you old bag!

00:20:59.400 --> 00:20:59.753
Let go of me, you drunk!
Shut your mouth! Stay out of this, you old bag!

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:00.750
Let go of me, you drunk!

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:07.871
Damn you, Kai! You still have work to do!

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:16.990
| wonder if Ichinose is really out here.

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:21.032
If I can, I want to hear that sound again.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:33.910
Wow, it's true. The keys are so heavy.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:37.438
It doesn't make any sound if you just play it normally.

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:40.280
They say there's only one like it in the entire world.

00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:42.000
It's Ajino Sousuke's specially-made piano.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.149
Yes, just as the lettering on it says, that was a piano made for me.
It's Ajino Sousuke's specially-made piano.

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:46.869
Yes, just as the lettering on it says, that was a piano made for me.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:50.036
Up until the accident anyway.

00:21:57.800 --> 00:22:02.670
With our current medical technology we will not be able to return his left arm to normal.

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:05.839
Of course, he should be able to live a normal life.

00:22:07.080 --> 00:22:09.196
But, as for being a pianist...

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:11.433
It's a terrible shame.

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:18.835
Though it has been two months since his accident,
Ajino Sousuke is still not allowing any visitors.

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:23.319
He lost his fiancée in that nightmare of an accident, and his career as a pianist—

00:22:38.360 --> 00:22:41.079
Even though I ended up getting a job as a college professor,

00:22:41.800 --> 00:22:45.953
no matter who I listened to, no one impressed me or moved me at all.

00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:49.315
Eventually, ten years after the accident,

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:53.630
| was stripped of my honorary title as professor emeritus.

00:22:56.880 --> 00:23:00.635
| wasn't sad or lonely for being estranged from the piano world.

00:23:01.640 --> 00:23:07.875
But for some reason, in the end I felt an urge to see
one more time the piano that I had given away.

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:11.830
Oh yeah, it was here. A really big piano.

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:15.710
She was always stripping on top of that piano.

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:19.476
Man, that dirty little girl would act like some rich man's daughter.

00:23:22.120 --> 00:23:26.000
Hey, you, wait just a second! You're looking for that piano, right?

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:28.991
Do you know where it is?

00:23:29.280 --> 00:23:34.480
If that's the one, I heard they abandoned it in the forest
behind the cabaret when they knocked it down.

00:24:15.960 --> 00:24:18.270
Why, back in that accident...

00:24:25.560 --> 00:24:27.915
Why couldn't I have died?

00:24:29.480 --> 00:24:30.550
It's been three years since then.

00:24:31.040 --> 00:24:34.078
And yet I still can't leave the area where that piano is.

00:24:35.320 --> 00:24:36.913
Even now it occasionally flashes through my mind.

00:24:37.360 --> 00:24:40.239
The unforgettable sound of that piano.

00:24:41.240 --> 00:24:44.358
If he can truly get sound from that piano...

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:46.877
Please let me hear it. That sound.

00:24:58.240 --> 00:25:02.598
No matter what, I need to take that child's words seriously.

00:25:04.200 --> 00:25:07.636
Geez, I amaze myself. What have I been reduced to?

00:25:37.160 --> 00:25:38.514
Th-This sound...

00:25:39.800 --> 00:25:42.679
I-It couldn't be...

00:25:44.920 --> 00:25:46.672
Could the piano truly be...

00:26:08.160 --> 00:26:09.036
Ichinose?

00:26:14.280 --> 00:26:15.270
This sound...

00:26:16.440 --> 00:26:18.078
The sound coming from that piano...

00:26:24.920 --> 00:26:26.831
It's my sound!

00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:06.116
Let go of me!

00:27:07.880 --> 00:27:08.711
Ichinose!

00:27:08.720 --> 00:27:08.959
Let go of me!

00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:09.472
Ichinose!
Let go of me!

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:13.118
Did you follow me all the way here, you drunk?!

00:27:13.120 --> 00:27:14.519
I'll kick your ass!

00:27:14.520 --> 00:27:16.511
Ichinose! Ichinose! Calm down!

00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:17.717
Let go of me! Let go, let go!

00:27:17.720 --> 00:27:18.755
It's me! It's Ajino!
Let go of me! Let go, let go!

00:27:19.280 --> 00:27:20.509
Let go of— Huh?

00:27:22.760 --> 00:27:23.955
A-Ajino?

00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:24.597
That's right.

00:27:24.960 --> 00:27:26.280
What are you—

00:27:26.640 --> 00:27:28.392
Why are you here?

00:27:28.880 --> 00:27:31.030
How should I explain this...

00:27:32.600 --> 00:27:34.750
The thing is, this is my piano.

00:27:35.280 --> 00:27:37.157
It's not yours! It's mine!

00:27:39.400 --> 00:27:42.358
That's right. Now, it's your piano.

00:27:43.160 --> 00:27:46.516
You're probably the only one who can play it in the entire world.

00:27:47.040 --> 00:27:48.235
Therefore, it's your piano.

00:27:51.560 --> 00:27:52.277
Ichinose...

00:28:00.040 --> 00:28:02.031
Will you play the piano with me?

00:28:04.920 --> 00:28:07.673
You have the chosen hands.

00:28:10.040 --> 00:28:11.951
The hands the piano chose.

00:28:16.040 --> 00:28:17.155
Piss off!

00:28:19.080 --> 00:28:21.913
Like I'd play the piano with you!

00:28:22.960 --> 00:28:27.955
| finally have time to enjoy myself and you come and
interrupt me... Do you even know what time it is?

00:28:28.960 --> 00:28:33.193
More importantly, Ajino, a piano is something you play alone.

00:28:38.200 --> 00:28:39.076
Ichinose...

00:28:42.080 --> 00:28:49.237
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart Piano Sonata No. 8 in A minor, K 310 Third
Movement (Presto) - Final Stanzas m100182808381083869828791079069010100

00:29:06.760 --> 00:29:08.751
Amazing!

00:29:10.640 --> 00:29:15.635
You're amazing, Amamiya! I've never heard such beautiful piano playing before!

00:29:15.880 --> 00:29:17.234
You can tone down the flattery, Kai-kun.

00:29:17.760 --> 00:29:19.239
| still have a long way to go.

00:29:19.840 --> 00:29:22.480
| can't hope to win the competition like this.

00:29:22.720 --> 00:29:23.994
Competition?

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:24.512
Yup.

00:29:25.280 --> 00:29:28.750
The All-Japan Student Piano Competition is taking place soon.

00:29:29.480 --> 00:29:33.030
There are several competitions, but the level of that one is the highest.

00:29:33.520 --> 00:29:36.512
They say it's the gateway to becoming a professional pianist.

00:29:36.760 --> 00:29:41.516
And you're gonna enter that, Amamiya? You really are something.

00:29:41.520 --> 00:29:43.272
| was just playing the qualifying song.

00:29:43.760 --> 00:29:46.354
Mozart's Piano Sonata 310.

00:29:46.640 --> 00:29:49.029
So that was Mozart?

00:29:49.760 --> 00:29:52.912
What are all those little squiggly things?

00:29:53.520 --> 00:29:57.115
That's the score, it's like blueprints for the music.

00:29:58.880 --> 00:30:02.157
If you can read the score, you'll be able to play any piece.

00:30:03.040 --> 00:30:07.034
Oh yeah! You should learn it too, Kai-kun.

00:30:07.760 --> 00:30:10.752
It's okay, really! Spare me the studying.

00:30:10.760 --> 00:30:11.397
But...

00:30:11.640 --> 00:30:13.074
Oh, that reminds me!

00:30:13.680 --> 00:30:16.559
That Ajino bastard showed up in the forest last night.

00:30:17.560 --> 00:30:22.191
He just came up and grabbed my arm and starting saying all this crazy stuff.

00:30:24.200 --> 00:30:28.558
To top it off, he asked if I would play the piano with him!

00:30:29.680 --> 00:30:31.193
It wasn't funny.

00:30:31.920 --> 00:30:38.394
Like I'd play the piano with that guy just like that. We're not even friends!

00:30:39.160 --> 00:30:40.036
He probably meant...

00:30:41.200 --> 00:30:42.031
He probably meant...

00:30:43.080 --> 00:30:45.594
...that he was offering to teach you piano.

00:30:46.920 --> 00:30:48.957
That's not funny either.

00:30:48.960 --> 00:30:52.351
| didn't ask him to do that; who does he think he is?

00:30:52.360 --> 00:30:53.475
But isn't it great?

00:30:54.800 --> 00:30:57.838
| asked him to do it and he refused.

00:30:59.440 --> 00:31:04.116
Why did you ask Ajino for something like that?
Amamiya, you can already play the piano!

00:31:05.240 --> 00:31:07.117
Just playing is no good.

00:31:08.560 --> 00:31:11.473
For me, it's essential to find a top-caliber mentor.

00:31:12.320 --> 00:31:14.357
Kai-kun, this is your chance!

00:31:14.760 --> 00:31:17.991
With an opportunity like this, you have to try and learn the piano for real!

00:31:18.360 --> 00:31:23.389
If Ajino-sensei asked something like that, then you must have a talent for the piano!

00:31:23.840 --> 00:31:26.229
Oh, and you don't need to worry about me.

00:31:26.720 --> 00:31:29.394
| don't really like Ajino-sensei that much anyway.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:31.752
And even though he refused me...

00:31:32.280 --> 00:31:36.638
If he told you he'd teach you, please don't worry about that and just let him teach you.

00:31:40.160 --> 00:31:43.232
D-D-Don't say such stupid things!

00:31:43.520 --> 00:31:48.515
Just shut up and listen! How dare you tell me what
to do? I don't want to be taught by anyone!

00:31:49.640 --> 00:31:54.794
Amamiya, you're just trying to push Ajino on me, aren't you!
Because you don't want to learn from him yourself!

00:31:55.040 --> 00:31:56.792
Th-That's not it at all, Kai-kun!

00:31:58.360 --> 00:32:02.035
Besides, my family doesn't have the money to pay for teaching.

00:32:05.680 --> 00:32:08.149
I'm sorry, but I'm different from you.

00:32:14.040 --> 00:32:17.556
But, Amamiya, aren't you a little too obsessed over Ajino?

00:32:17.880 --> 00:32:20.759
Sure, he may have been a great pianist in the past...

00:32:21.760 --> 00:32:26.197
But now he's just a cheap music teacher who gets on everyone's bad side.

00:32:26.960 --> 00:32:30.635
Kai-kun, if you want, I'll teach you piano.

00:32:31.320 --> 00:32:34.153
Of course I won't charge you. See, that Mozart piece from before—

00:32:34.160 --> 00:32:37.198
Thank you, Amamiya, but it's fine because I've already memorized it.

00:32:37.680 --> 00:32:38.590
See ya!

00:32:58.360 --> 00:33:00.237
Will you play the piano with me?

00:33:01.200 --> 00:33:04.477
Why did I say that to him?

00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:09.356
| was supposed to have cut ties with that world already.

00:33:13.960 --> 00:33:17.954
Music Room

00:33:25.760 --> 00:33:26.591
Ichinose?

00:33:31.640 --> 00:33:35.270
That's Mozart's Piano Sonata 310.

00:33:40.480 --> 00:33:46.237
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart Piano Sonata No. 8 in A minor, K 310 Third
Movement (Presto) - Final Stanzas m100182808381083869828791079069010100

00:33:46.640 --> 00:33:48.392
A-Ajino...

00:33:48.760 --> 00:33:50.512
He hasn't gone home yet?

00:33:51.400 --> 00:33:56.759
You've got some guts. You skip school and yet
you come to the music room to play around?

00:33:57.480 --> 00:33:59.391
Or did you come to see me?

00:33:59.800 --> 00:34:01.393
Like I'd ever do that!

00:34:01.880 --> 00:34:04.235
| just came in to take a look at Mozart's face.

00:34:06.240 --> 00:34:07.753
Is that Mozart?

00:34:10.480 --> 00:34:11.834
That's Beethoven.

00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:13.832
Ludwig van Beethoven Bagatelle in A minor, WoO 59
Fur Elise m1001828 08381083869828791079069010100

00:34:13.840 --> 00:34:15.353
Speaking of Beethoven... Ludwig van Beethoven Bagatelle in A
minor, WoO 59 Fur Elise m1001828 08381083869828791079069010100

00:34:15.360 --> 00:34:19.240
Ludwig van Beethoven Bagatelle in A minor, WoO 59
Fur Elise m1001828 08381083869828791079069010100

00:34:19.240 --> 00:34:19.320
That's the song from Rei-chan"s music box. Ludwig van Beethoven Bagatelle
in A minor, WoO 59 Fur Elise m1001828 08381083869828791079069010100

00:34:19.320 --> 00:34:21.231
That's the song from Rei-chan's music box.

00:34:21.600 --> 00:34:24.479
He has plenty of other famous songs.

00:34:24.840 --> 00:34:25.989
For example...

00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:31.358
Ludwig van Beethoven Symphony No. 5 in C minor, Op. 67 First
Movement (Allegro con brio) m100182808381083869828791079069010100

00:34:31.480 --> 00:34:34.598
This is called "Fate," from his fifth symphony.

00:34:37.000 --> 00:34:38.991
| know that one!

00:34:39.240 --> 00:34:41.470
Bam-bam-bam bam, right?

00:34:41.760 --> 00:34:44.479
Man, I know a whole bunch of songs.

00:34:45.360 --> 00:34:47.192
Okay, Ajino, how about this guy?

00:34:47.200 --> 00:34:48.759
That's Mendelssohn.

00:34:49.120 --> 00:34:55.116
Felix Mendelssohn-Bartholdy A Midsummer Night's Dream,
Op. 61 Wedding March m100182808381083869828791079069010100

00:35:01.360 --> 00:35:02.714
| know this! I know this!

00:35:05.840 --> 00:35:07.877
Hey, what about him?

00:35:10.160 --> 00:35:10.911
That's Chopin.

00:35:11.920 --> 00:35:14.639
Chopin also has a large number of famous songs...

00:35:16.040 --> 00:35:16.916
For example, the Minute Waltz.

00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:18.513
Frédéric Chopin Waltz in D flat major, Op. 64, No. 1Petit chien (Little Dog) -
Minute Waltz m1001828 08381083869828791079069010100 For example, the Minute Waltz.

00:35:18.520 --> 00:35:22.912
Frédéric Chopin Waltz in D flat major, Op. 64, No. 1Petit chien
(Little Dog) - Minute Waltz m100182808381083869828791079069010100

00:35:35.800 --> 00:35:41.318
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart Piano Sonata No. 8 in A minor, K 310 First Movement
(Allegro maestoso) - Initial Stanzas m100182808381083869828791079069010100

00:35:43.920 --> 00:35:47.072
See, you can't even get a word in.

00:35:47.080 --> 00:35:51.313
| know, I've never seen Shuuhei-san so serious before.

00:35:53.680 --> 00:35:55.034
Ajino-sensei...

00:35:58.200 --> 00:35:59.634
instead of me...

00:36:02.800 --> 00:36:04.154
he chose Kai-kun.

00:36:12.080 --> 00:36:13.593
This is Beethoven.

00:36:16.040 --> 00:36:18.077
And when you think of Beethoven,

00:36:19.080 --> 00:36:21.071
how can you forget...

00:36:21.480 --> 00:36:23.471
Fate!

00:36:29.600 --> 00:36:31.432
That'll wake you up.

00:36:31.840 --> 00:36:32.955
And now...

00:36:33.680 --> 00:36:36.115
And this is Chopin: the Minute Waltz.

00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:47.640
Huh? What happened?

00:36:55.000 --> 00:36:58.880
But I can play Mozart and Mendelssohn just fine...

00:37:10.720 --> 00:37:13.599
Why only when I play Chopin?

00:37:15.040 --> 00:37:19.113
That Kai! He's skipped school five days straight.

00:37:19.120 --> 00:37:21.714
I'm kicking his ass when he shows up.

00:37:24.160 --> 00:37:27.869
What happened to Kai-kun?
He's taken five days off from school.

00:37:31.280 --> 00:37:32.634
Oh! Kai-kun!

00:37:46.560 --> 00:37:48.915
Ichinose, do you have something to say to me?

00:37:50.880 --> 00:37:53.156
Sensei, Chopin...

00:37:54.400 --> 00:37:55.879
Please teach me Chopin!

00:37:56.880 --> 00:37:59.076
| can't play the Minute Waltz.

00:37:59.080 --> 00:38:01.151
| can play everything else just fine,

00:38:01.520 --> 00:38:03.670
but I can't play Chopin at all.

00:38:04.640 --> 00:38:06.916
But I definitely want to play it.

00:38:06.920 --> 00:38:08.957
Please show me how to play it.

00:38:09.560 --> 00:38:11.437
No problem, I'll show you.

00:38:12.320 --> 00:38:14.038
But I do have one condition.

00:38:14.680 --> 00:38:16.159
I-| don't have any money.

00:38:17.960 --> 00:38:23.433
The condition is that you are not to run away until you're able to play it.

00:38:24.440 --> 00:38:27.080
Not from me and not from playing piano.

00:38:27.720 --> 00:38:29.438
Wh-What kind of condition is that?

00:38:30.240 --> 00:38:33.471
If you're okay with that, come back here after school tomorrow.

00:38:35.920 --> 00:38:39.959
I'll just say this: I'm not planning on learning from you for free!

00:38:50.200 --> 00:38:53.238
Geez. It's you, Amamiya.

00:38:53.720 --> 00:38:56.951
| apologize. I didn't mean to, but I heard it all.

00:38:58.000 --> 00:39:03.234
Oh man, this is bad. I guess that makes me a big liar.

00:39:03.240 --> 00:39:05.197
But I'm glad.

00:39:05.880 --> 00:39:08.759
You get to learn piano from Ajino-sensei.

00:39:10.400 --> 00:39:13.950
You know, even though you said you weren't considering his offer.

00:39:15.480 --> 00:39:17.232
| knew he couldn't turn him down.

00:39:18.040 --> 00:39:21.476
| mean, he is a former top-rate pianist after all.

00:39:22.520 --> 00:39:27.913
I'm not really accepting his offer, there's just this one song I can't play.

00:39:28.600 --> 00:39:33.390
In any case, if it means Ajino-sensei will be your teacher then it's a good thing.

00:39:33.400 --> 00:39:35.994
No way. He's not going to teach me forever.

00:39:36.880 --> 00:39:39.759
Fine, fine. It's just a good thing, that's all.

00:39:40.280 --> 00:39:41.031
See you tomorrow!

00:39:46.560 --> 00:39:52.750
It's good that such a good thing happened, isn't
it? It's nothing I need to be upset about, is it?

00:39:58.200 --> 00:40:00.271
Kai-kun didn't do anything bad.

00:40:01.760 --> 00:40:03.671
Why am I so upset about it?

00:40:07.200 --> 00:40:09.430
What's with me?

00:40:14.440 --> 00:40:17.398
Good morning!

00:40:19.920 --> 00:40:20.671
They're fighting!

00:40:20.680 --> 00:40:21.272
A fight! A fight! A fight in grade 5 classroom 3!
They're fighting!

00:40:21.280 --> 00:40:23.715
A fight! A fight! A fight in grade 5 classroom 3!

00:40:23.720 --> 00:40:26.155
Kai and Kinpira are having a really loud fight!

00:40:28.720 --> 00:40:30.438
Don't play dumb!

00:40:30.440 --> 00:40:34.070
| heard that you've been cutting class because your mom ran off with a customer!

00:40:34.240 --> 00:40:35.958
Like I'd even know that!

00:40:36.240 --> 00:40:38.436
Tell me, you jerk!

00:40:38.440 --> 00:40:39.953
Shut your mouth, you fat pig!

00:40:41.800 --> 00:40:43.473
Kai-kun, don't fight him!

00:40:44.080 --> 00:40:45.593
Eat this, fat ass!

00:40:48.480 --> 00:40:49.709
Kai-kun, don't use your fist!

00:40:49.720 --> 00:40:53.600
Let me go, Amamiya. I'm gonna strangle this pig today once and for all!

00:40:54.840 --> 00:40:58.117
Did you forget? You have a lesson with Ajino-sensei today!

00:40:58.640 --> 00:41:01.109
It'd be really bad if you hurt your hand!

00:41:01.760 --> 00:41:04.639
You can't fight with your hands anymore!

00:41:05.240 --> 00:41:07.117
Let go of me, Amamiya.

00:41:07.840 --> 00:41:09.638
So stop fighting, okay?

00:41:10.240 --> 00:41:11.833
| said let go of me!

00:41:16.880 --> 00:41:17.631
Kai-kun...

00:41:18.400 --> 00:41:22.155
What I do with my hands is my decision!

00:41:22.160 --> 00:41:25.516
That's true, but you have an important lesson to prepare for.

00:41:25.520 --> 00:41:26.396
Shut up already!

00:41:26.760 --> 00:41:28.478
It's different now.

00:41:28.480 --> 00:41:29.914
It's none of your business.

00:41:30.240 --> 00:41:31.639
I'm just worried about you...

00:41:32.120 --> 00:41:35.272
Worried?! Worry about yourself, Amamiya!

00:41:35.920 --> 00:41:41.552
If your hands are so important, then you'd better protect
those weak, girly hands of yours with your life!

00:41:57.680 --> 00:41:59.910
| understand. That's what I'll do.

00:42:01.440 --> 00:42:03.875
I'm only going to worry about myself from now on.

00:42:12.840 --> 00:42:16.629
Hey, tell me, Kai! What's this about a lesson?

00:42:16.640 --> 00:42:20.520
Shut up! I'm not telling you nothing!

00:42:20.720 --> 00:42:22.597
Mr. Peas-for-nuts!

00:42:23.280 --> 00:42:25.317
You...

00:42:26.040 --> 00:42:27.678
I'll beat you to death!

00:42:29.800 --> 00:42:31.552
Hey!

00:42:32.040 --> 00:42:35.078
Stop that fighting!

00:42:35.080 --> 00:42:38.357
Hey! Kanehira-kun! Ichinose-kun!

00:42:38.360 --> 00:42:41.830
Koutama Dormitory
m100132803381033849328591059049010100

00:42:43.800 --> 00:42:45.837
So this is where you live, Ajino?

00:42:46.240 --> 00:42:46.911
Ichinose.

00:42:48.840 --> 00:42:50.558
The lesson room is this way.

00:42:52.360 --> 00:42:55.716
It's a prefab room that my landlord built for his daughter to practice piano.

00:42:56.480 --> 00:43:01.475
It's just being used for storage now, but since it's fully
soundproofed, you can practice without worrying.

00:43:20.840 --> 00:43:23.719
For starters, you need to get used to playing on a normal piano.

00:43:24.600 --> 00:43:28.389
Okay, Ichinose. I'm going to play now, so try and remember the music.

00:43:37.880 --> 00:43:39.917
Th-That's not a song.

00:43:41.480 --> 00:43:44.359
It's a practice piece for your fingers. It's a musical scale.

00:43:45.360 --> 00:43:46.156
Try and play it.

00:43:52.520 --> 00:43:58.755
Yes, start off slowly. Continue like that. Just try to keep the sound consistent.

00:44:03.400 --> 00:44:08.315
Keep repeating the same phrase on different scales
over and over. It's exercising your fingers.

00:44:09.320 --> 00:44:13.029
Because it's monotonous and doesn't have a
melody, you can keep your feelings out of it.

00:44:13.680 --> 00:44:16.957
It's probably incredibly boring for you.

00:44:17.680 --> 00:44:21.071
| can't do this. My head feels funny.

00:44:21.440 --> 00:44:24.432
Somehow the keys are starting to look distorted.

00:44:24.960 --> 00:44:27.600
They're getting all distorted, the keys...

00:44:34.680 --> 00:44:37.957
What's the matter, Ichinose? You can call it quits if you want.

00:44:39.200 --> 00:44:44.957
Playing piano just for fun is really enjoyable, but lessons are a lot of work.

00:44:47.120 --> 00:44:50.590
Amamiya must have done so much of this.

00:44:52.800 --> 00:44:56.998
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart Piano Sonata No. 8 in A minor, K 310 First Movement
(Allegro maestoso) - Final Stanzas m100182808381083869828791079069010100

00:44:59.200 --> 00:45:01.077
I'm different from Kai-kun.

00:45:03.120 --> 00:45:05.111
| don't play piano just for fun.

00:45:07.560 --> 00:45:10.200
My goal is to become a pianist.

00:45:12.760 --> 00:45:14.751
I'm different from Kai-kun!

00:45:26.600 --> 00:45:27.999
Hey, isn't this cute?

00:45:28.000 --> 00:45:29.354
Where did you buy it?

00:45:33.400 --> 00:45:34.754
Good morning, Amamiya.

00:45:40.760 --> 00:45:45.038
I-I'm sorry for saying those horrible things yesterday. Please forgive me.

00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:48.998
You don't need to apologize, Ichinose-kun.

00:45:51.160 --> 00:45:56.792
| was wrong for meddling with your business.
| shouldn't have been so worried about you.

00:45:57.560 --> 00:46:02.031
| know how difficult lessons are now. That's why, you—

00:46:02.040 --> 00:46:04.316
They aren't a big deal if you have a goal in sight.

00:46:11.880 --> 00:46:12.790
Amamiya...

00:46:28.440 --> 00:46:33.594
This is so boring. How many more days do I have to keep doing this?

00:46:34.800 --> 00:46:36.950
I've already pissed off Amamiya.

00:46:51.200 --> 00:46:52.599
There's a skylight.

00:46:53.680 --> 00:46:57.116
That's right. I guess the moon comes out wherever you are.

00:47:01.880 --> 00:47:04.349
All-Japan Student Piano Competition?

00:47:05.000 --> 00:47:10.074
Yeah. It looks like Amamiya Shuuhei-kun from my class is going to enter it.

00:47:10.360 --> 00:47:13.239
It's an honor just to appear in it, isn't it?

00:47:13.240 --> 00:47:14.639
Yeah, I suppose.

00:47:14.640 --> 00:47:18.315
Seeing as it's my homeroom class, I'm so proud!

00:47:23.880 --> 00:47:28.954
Well, the scenery is not quite the same, but...

00:47:37.520 --> 00:47:38.840
This is the forest.

00:47:42.160 --> 00:47:45.755
And this is the piano in the forest.

00:47:51.880 --> 00:47:55.350
Huh? The sound is a little different.

00:47:55.920 --> 00:47:57.752
The piano in the forest was more...

00:47:58.880 --> 00:48:00.871
Just a little bit more...

00:48:02.040 --> 00:48:04.156
There we go. Like this...

00:48:08.280 --> 00:48:09.873
A-Awesome!

00:48:11.800 --> 00:48:14.553
Faster! Faster!

00:48:15.000 --> 00:48:17.196
More! More!

00:48:17.440 --> 00:48:18.635
More!

00:48:19.760 --> 00:48:20.511
That's enough.

00:48:22.920 --> 00:48:24.957
Ajino! How long have you been there?

00:48:27.160 --> 00:48:29.071
That's enough, Ichinose.

00:48:31.840 --> 00:48:32.796
You pass.

00:48:34.920 --> 00:48:38.834
| did it! Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:48:38.840 --> 00:48:39.318
Continue playing like that and try to play the Minute Waltz.

00:48:39.320 --> 00:48:41.596
Yes! Yes! Yes!
Continue playing like that and try to play the Minute Waltz.

00:48:41.600 --> 00:48:42.032
Continue playing like that and try to play the Minute Waltz.

00:48:43.840 --> 00:48:48.152
B-But you haven't taught me how to play Chopin yet.

00:48:48.840 --> 00:48:51.673
Just give it a shot. You should be able to play it now.

00:48:54.600 --> 00:48:56.477
| told you, I won't be able to!

00:48:57.480 --> 00:48:58.675
Concentrate.

00:49:12.440 --> 00:49:13.236
It's true.

00:49:13.880 --> 00:49:17.714
| can really play it. I'm playing Chopin.

00:49:18.240 --> 00:49:23.189
You don't use your strength to play Chopin. Rather,
it requires flexibility and motion control.

00:49:23.760 --> 00:49:26.957
Once you can play a normal piano, you can play Chopin.

00:49:29.400 --> 00:49:30.470
| did it!

00:49:30.760 --> 00:49:34.355
| did it! I did it! I played Chopin!

00:49:34.880 --> 00:49:35.995
That's great, isn't it?

00:49:36.640 --> 00:49:37.994
Ajino, we have a deal.

00:49:38.840 --> 00:49:42.515
| told you. I'm not planning on learning from you for free.

00:49:42.880 --> 00:49:47.158
Now it's my turn to do something you want. What would you like me to do?

00:49:50.120 --> 00:49:52.634
Of course, it has to be something that doesn't cost me any money.

00:49:54.280 --> 00:49:55.156
In that case,

00:49:56.480 --> 00:50:00.030
I'd like you to enter the All-Japan Student Piano Competition.

00:50:03.160 --> 00:50:06.676
The qualifying song is Mozart's K?chel 310.

00:50:07.280 --> 00:50:11.911
W-Wait just a second. You're saying I'm going to appear in a piano competition?

00:50:11.920 --> 00:50:12.557
That's right.

00:50:12.760 --> 00:50:14.159
A-Are you serious?

00:50:14.160 --> 00:50:14.752
Of course.

00:50:22.920 --> 00:50:26.879
| could never imagine myself entering a competition!

00:50:27.640 --> 00:50:33.431
Only rich boys and girls who've been taking lessons
since they were babies enter those competitions.

00:50:33.920 --> 00:50:37.436
Not gonna do it. I can't grant such a ridiculous request.

00:50:37.960 --> 00:50:40.839
| see. I'm disappointed but I guess there's nothing I can do.

00:50:40.840 --> 00:50:45.391
Just give me something more realistic. I'll put my heart into it.

00:50:45.920 --> 00:50:47.319
There's nothing else I particularly want.

00:50:51.040 --> 00:50:53.350
H-H-Hold on!

00:50:53.360 --> 00:51:01.199
What do you mean, nothing? Think harder, there must
be something! Cleaning, errands, walking your dog!

00:51:01.680 --> 00:51:05.674
| can do those things without your assistance.

00:51:07.000 --> 00:51:11.676
Even if you were to put all your heart into them, |
can do the cleaning and stuff just as well as you.

00:51:15.440 --> 00:51:16.760
Besides, I don't have a dog.

00:51:20.560 --> 00:51:21.470
Wait!

00:51:27.720 --> 00:51:28.516
All right.

00:51:29.240 --> 00:51:32.870
I'm not happy about it, but I'll enter the competition!

00:51:33.480 --> 00:51:34.879
Are you sure you're okay with it?

00:51:35.240 --> 00:51:37.993
If you're reluctant, it would be better to just call it off.

00:51:38.280 --> 00:51:41.398
Well I don't have a choice, do I? You don't have any other requests...

00:51:42.960 --> 00:51:47.352
The qualifier for the competition is in ten days. I'll take care of the registration.

00:51:48.160 --> 00:51:52.393
| guess I should just bang on the keys and make a fool of myself, huh?

00:51:53.760 --> 00:51:56.400
I'll be looking forward to that.

00:52:05.520 --> 00:52:06.396
This can't be happening.

00:52:10.040 --> 00:52:13.795
Your lesson today starts at five. Don't keep the teacher waiting, okay?

00:52:14.440 --> 00:52:15.236
| understand.

00:52:16.160 --> 00:52:21.155
Your grandmother is starting to feel much better, so we'll be leaving here soon.

00:52:23.200 --> 00:52:28.070
Are you surprised? I'm thinking that we can move
back to Tokyo right after the competition.

00:52:28.920 --> 00:52:31.958
| see. After the competition.

00:52:36.280 --> 00:52:36.951
With Kai-kun...

00:52:38.640 --> 00:52:42.793
No, that doesn't matter. I have to focus on the competition!

00:52:43.680 --> 00:52:45.034
Ichinose-kun...

00:52:45.920 --> 00:52:47.957
Ichinose-kun didn't come again?

00:52:47.960 --> 00:52:48.950
He's cutting.

00:52:50.280 --> 00:52:52.078
| wonder what he's been up to.

00:52:52.080 --> 00:52:56.836
Kai-kun, are you playing the piano in the forest again?

00:52:59.480 --> 00:53:03.553
| think that fooling around on that would be a lot of fun.

00:53:04.960 --> 00:53:09.955
But that's right. It's as you said, we live in different worlds.

00:53:19.560 --> 00:53:21.119
What's wrong, Namie-san?

00:53:21.600 --> 00:53:22.874
Shuuhei-san...

00:53:26.360 --> 00:53:34.360
Well, we wanted to keep it a secret from you, but your father
arranged for Ajino-sensei to be a judge in the competition.

00:53:35.880 --> 00:53:37.871
Huh? Sensei? Why?

00:53:38.200 --> 00:53:45.072
He figured that there's no way he can ignore you once he hears you play the piano.

00:53:45.480 --> 00:53:48.757
He'll never accept that offer.

00:53:49.160 --> 00:53:54.633
Yeah, I just got a message from your father saying he'd refused.

00:53:55.600 --> 00:53:56.396
| knew it.

00:53:56.760 --> 00:54:00.515
And the reason Ajino-sensei gave for turning it down was...

00:54:01.480 --> 00:54:05.030
He said he's teaching a student who will be participating in the competition.

00:54:06.800 --> 00:54:11.033
Since he couldn't be a fair judge, he turned it down.

00:54:14.800 --> 00:54:15.676
What do you mean?

00:54:16.360 --> 00:54:21.036
| don't know. But he said that's definitely what Ajino said.

00:54:24.800 --> 00:54:25.517
Kai-kun...

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:32.514
Shuuhei-san, wait right there!

00:54:33.200 --> 00:54:37.034
If Ajino-sensei has a student, then it has to be Kai-kun!

00:54:38.400 --> 00:54:39.515
| was wrong about him.

00:54:40.440 --> 00:54:45.196
Could Kai-kun be serious enough about the piano
that he's going to participate in the competition?

00:55:08.160 --> 00:55:10.595
What are you gonna do about it, huh?

00:55:11.240 --> 00:55:12.833
It's your fault, you know.

00:55:13.360 --> 00:55:14.714
What's all that ruckus about?

00:55:15.240 --> 00:55:17.914
It looks like they caught some kid.

00:55:21.000 --> 00:55:24.356
So, what you gonna do, huh?

00:55:24.880 --> 00:55:27.440
D-Didn't I apologize already?

00:55:27.760 --> 00:55:34.473
You think an apology is enough? My pants got all dirty because you bumped into me.

00:55:35.360 --> 00:55:39.752
I'm gonna need ¥ 100,000 from you to pay the cleaning bill.

00:55:41.240 --> 00:55:43.959
I-It won't cost 100,000 for a stain that small...

00:55:44.360 --> 00:55:48.718
It will cost you 100,000. And you're gonna pay for it right here!

00:55:50.400 --> 00:55:51.071
I-n

00:55:52.160 --> 00:55:54.720
What are you looking at? Huh?

00:55:55.240 --> 00:55:57.629
| came here to see Ichinose Kai-kun!

00:55:57.960 --> 00:55:59.598
Kai?

00:56:01.840 --> 00:56:04.036
What do you need Kai for?!

00:56:10.400 --> 00:56:13.153
What are you doing with my important customer?

00:56:14.400 --> 00:56:16.676
| wasn't doing anything! We were just messing around.

00:56:17.680 --> 00:56:18.556
Are you all right?

00:56:20.240 --> 00:56:26.031
What's with you, Rei-chan? I don't care how broke you are,
don't tell me you're taking a brat like this as a client.

00:56:26.520 --> 00:56:30.434
Don't talk trash. He's Kai's close friend.

00:56:33.680 --> 00:56:37.150
Kai, your friend is here. Come outside.

00:56:37.880 --> 00:56:39.917
You're Amamiya Shuuhei-kun, aren't you?

00:56:40.800 --> 00:56:41.676
Y-Yes!

00:56:42.560 --> 00:56:44.949
I'm Reiko, Kai's mother.

00:56:48.960 --> 00:56:49.950
Amamiyal!

00:56:51.640 --> 00:56:52.436
Kai-kun...

00:56:56.080 --> 00:56:56.956
From here?

00:56:57.960 --> 00:57:01.840
Yeah, I climb out this window and walk to the piano.

00:57:02.280 --> 00:57:03.190
Climb?

00:57:03.480 --> 00:57:05.312
| climb down that tree.

00:57:09.920 --> 00:57:10.910
Not bad, huh?

00:57:12.160 --> 00:57:16.313
Kai fell out of that window when he was three years old.

00:57:18.480 --> 00:57:18.958
Here.

00:57:19.960 --> 00:57:20.711
Thank you.

00:57:22.120 --> 00:57:22.712
Uhm...

00:57:23.800 --> 00:57:25.438
He fell out of the window?

00:57:25.440 --> 00:57:28.717
Exactly! We searched all over for him thinking he might have died.

00:57:29.120 --> 00:57:31.953
And where do you think this guy was?

00:57:33.360 --> 00:57:35.590
He was playing on top of that piano.

00:57:37.000 --> 00:57:42.996
The trees of the forest protected him. And that's when that piano became his toy.

00:57:44.240 --> 00:57:48.632
Every morning and every night, whenever he was free.
He'd even stay all night sometimes, he was addicted!

00:57:49.520 --> 00:57:51.113
Don't say I was addicted.

00:57:52.880 --> 00:57:56.271
I'm just doing as I've been told, learning to play the piano.

00:57:57.080 --> 00:57:57.876
But, to Kai-kun...

00:58:09.280 --> 00:58:10.509
To Kai-kun, piano is...

00:58:15.600 --> 00:58:17.477
You play piano too, right, Shuu-chan?

00:58:18.160 --> 00:58:19.912
| heard all about you from Kai.

00:58:20.280 --> 00:58:22.396
He said he made a friend who plays the piano.

00:58:22.920 --> 00:58:25.560
Keep being Kai's good friend, okay?

00:58:26.360 --> 00:58:27.680
<i>Y-Yes, ma'am.</i>

00:58:29.240 --> 00:58:31.675
Rei-chan, it's time for work. Get dressed.

00:58:31.880 --> 00:58:32.915
Okay.

00:58:43.080 --> 00:58:45.310
Amamiya, let's go outside.

00:58:51.080 --> 00:58:54.038
You're entering the competition, right?

00:58:54.920 --> 00:59:01.917
I-I was planning on explaining all that! I don't want you
to be upset, so I need to explain the reason why.

00:59:05.400 --> 00:59:07.596
I'm not upset.

00:59:09.160 --> 00:59:12.357
The piano was always my opponent when I was a little kid.

00:59:13.200 --> 00:59:16.795
| had to sacrifice so many things for my lessons.

00:59:17.600 --> 00:59:20.956
It was my curse to bear, being born into a family with a history as pianists.

00:59:21.960 --> 00:59:26.352
But there's nothing I can do about it, it's my fate.

00:59:27.320 --> 00:59:30.312
That's what the piano is for me.

00:59:31.240 --> 00:59:37.111
| feel like I understand a little bit about what the piano is for you.

00:59:38.080 --> 00:59:39.115
Amamiya...

00:59:42.120 --> 00:59:44.236
That's why we can give everything we've got to this competition.

00:59:44.480 --> 00:59:49.873
Wait, listen to my reasons! I'm not really going to take it all that seriously!

00:59:50.120 --> 00:59:51.713
| don't care about your reasons.

00:59:52.640 --> 00:59:55.519
You have to give it your all if you're entering the competition.

00:59:56.120 --> 01:00:02.719
That's the least you can do for my sake and for the sake of the competition.

01:00:03.840 --> 01:00:05.353
Promise me you will, okay?

01:00:06.840 --> 01:00:09.400
Okay. I understand.

01:00:27.120 --> 01:00:31.512
You won't make it to school tomorrow if you're wandering around at this hour.

01:00:32.800 --> 01:00:33.870
Say, Ajino...

01:00:34.760 --> 01:00:40.153
Could you help me be ready to give the competition everything I've got?

01:00:41.280 --> 01:00:45.433
Of course. That's why I just finished adjusting the sound.

01:00:46.760 --> 01:00:47.670
This is the score.

01:00:50.920 --> 01:00:54.197
And this is a recording of it being performed.

01:00:55.440 --> 01:00:58.034
It's an old tape, so the quality isn't great.

01:00:58.680 --> 01:01:02.071
But there's no mistaking that it's Mozart's Piano Sonata K?chel 310.

01:01:04.320 --> 01:01:06.960
Is that the old Ajino playing?

01:01:07.600 --> 01:01:11.070
Yes. Much better than I can play now.

01:01:21.480 --> 01:01:23.835
Ichinose-kun, go ahead and read the next line.

01:01:27.120 --> 01:01:29.236
Is Ichinose-kun sleeping again?

01:01:29.840 --> 01:01:31.831
Hey! Wake up, Kai!

01:01:32.240 --> 01:01:33.469
| said wake up!

01:01:34.240 --> 01:01:35.230
Hey!

01:01:49.320 --> 01:01:50.116
That's enough.

01:01:53.000 --> 01:01:55.719
You've gotten pretty good at copying my style.

01:01:55.720 --> 01:01:56.994
You can tell?

01:01:57.000 --> 01:01:58.991
Do you enjoy copying others?

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:01.752
| just enjoy playing well.

01:02:02.120 --> 01:02:04.396
Give me back the tape I let you borrow earlier.

01:02:13.760 --> 01:02:16.479
Don't listen to this anymore!

01:02:17.360 --> 01:02:18.509
That's an important tape!

01:02:21.120 --> 01:02:25.910
Don't copy others, don't play the piano like others. Play your own piano!

01:02:27.120 --> 01:02:29.919
| want to hear your own K?chel 310.

01:02:31.680 --> 01:02:34.035
If you don't start playing your own style of music...

01:02:34.560 --> 01:02:38.519
Mozart is going to come from the grave and say, "Give me back my score!"

01:02:40.240 --> 01:02:44.996
| can't really tell the difference between my piano
playing and someone else's piano playing!

01:02:46.520 --> 01:02:52.436
| know. But if you truly play your own piano, you'll
be able to savor the best feeling imaginable.

01:02:59.200 --> 01:03:01.510
Just what exactly is my own piano?

01:03:06.400 --> 01:03:11.190
If you're not going to play your own piano, do you think I can have my score back?

01:03:12.040 --> 01:03:13.439
He's here already!

01:03:14.080 --> 01:03:16.913
Shit!

01:03:27.600 --> 01:03:29.716
So, can you play your own piano?

01:03:30.440 --> 01:03:32.238
You're gonna embarrass yourself at the concert.

01:03:32.600 --> 01:03:35.240
You know, maybe you shouldn't enter after all.

01:03:36.240 --> 01:03:38.436
Each day there are more of you!

01:03:40.120 --> 01:03:41.997
Screw you all!

01:04:14.480 --> 01:04:15.709
And so, we've both...

01:04:17.400 --> 01:04:19.038
made it to the day of the competition.

01:04:23.880 --> 01:04:26.759
Are you ready? Let's get going.

01:04:30.920 --> 01:04:32.797
Kai is such a mean kid.

01:04:33.280 --> 01:04:36.796
He didn't even mention the competition until yesterday!

01:04:37.160 --> 01:04:38.275
Is that true?

01:04:39.000 --> 01:04:42.550
Because if I told her, Rei-chan would be all happy and stuff.

01:04:43.920 --> 01:04:46.912
See, it's not even something to get all happy about.

01:04:46.920 --> 01:04:51.312
Why not? I'm so excited that you're gonna be in the competition, Kai!

01:04:51.320 --> 01:04:56.315
56th South Central Region All Japan Student Piano
Competition m1001528 05381053869528791079069010100

01:04:57.760 --> 01:05:01.879
Only one person is going to make it to the nationals from today's regional competition.

01:05:02.200 --> 01:05:03.429
Nationals?

01:05:04.280 --> 01:05:08.160
Yes, that is where they decide who the best pianist in all Japan is.

01:05:08.320 --> 01:05:09.515
The best in all Japan?

01:05:10.280 --> 01:05:14.194
To think that Kai would be entering a contest that ultimately decides the best in Japan.

01:05:14.200 --> 01:05:16.077
Stop saying such stupid stuff!

01:05:16.840 --> 01:05:19.309
Like I'm trying to be the best in Japan...

01:05:21.960 --> 01:05:24.270
Is Mozart's ghost still haunting you?

01:05:24.560 --> 01:05:28.349
Wipe that smirk off your face! Just whose fault do you think that is?!

01:05:29.040 --> 01:05:29.950
Is something wrong?

01:05:30.560 --> 01:05:34.474
I-I'm gonna go check out the contestants' green room.

01:05:34.840 --> 01:05:37.036
Amamiya might be there already.

01:05:42.120 --> 01:05:44.430
Amamiya, Amamiya...

01:05:46.240 --> 01:05:48.117
| guess he's not here yet.

01:05:51.680 --> 01:05:53.114
This sucks!

01:05:54.200 --> 01:05:57.636
Why does Amamiya Shuuhei get to be in the South Central region?

01:05:58.000 --> 01:06:00.640
Isn't he from the Kantou region, Shiraishi?

01:06:00.880 --> 01:06:03.713
Yes, according to data from six months ago, he was.

01:06:03.720 --> 01:06:06.109
He'll place first if he's entering!

01:06:06.640 --> 01:06:10.110
We won't know that until the end.

01:06:10.520 --> 01:06:11.476
| do know!

01:06:12.480 --> 01:06:15.393
| mean, isn't he Amamiya Youichirou's son?

01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:18.071
The winner's already decided no matter what we do.

01:06:18.760 --> 01:06:21.115
There's no point in even entering this competition!

01:06:21.120 --> 01:06:22.474
Then, why don't you quit?

01:06:23.280 --> 01:06:25.112
You've been blathering this whole time!

01:06:25.880 --> 01:06:30.636
| don't care if you're nervous. Just quit saying such
ridiculous things with that foul mouth of yours!

01:06:31.280 --> 01:06:36.992
I'm not saying ridiculous things. It's already been decided
that Amamiya Shuuhei will win this competition.

01:06:37.000 --> 01:06:37.876
Maybe.

01:06:38.800 --> 01:06:45.399
But that's not for you to say. The only one who
decides if Amamiya wins is Amamiya himself!

01:06:46.040 --> 01:06:48.680
He'll win with his own strength.

01:06:59.560 --> 01:07:00.755
Amamiyal!

01:07:03.680 --> 01:07:04.670
Oh, Kai-kun!

01:07:07.280 --> 01:07:08.554
Kai-kun, you're early.

01:07:08.560 --> 01:07:09.197
Yeah!

01:07:11.320 --> 01:07:13.197
Who is that guy?

01:07:14.680 --> 01:07:16.557
Nonomura Hanayo-sensei.

01:07:17.080 --> 01:07:19.037
Yamaguchi Chie-sensei.

01:07:19.320 --> 01:07:21.197
Hiramoto Ryuuichi-sensei.

01:07:21.960 --> 01:07:25.919
Those twelve professors will be the judges.

01:07:27.200 --> 01:07:27.314
Elementary

01:07:27.320 --> 01:07:30.312
Now begins the elementary school section of our competition.
Elementary

01:07:30.320 --> 01:07:30.718
Elementary

01:07:31.200 --> 01:07:33.589
#1, Enomoto Rika-san.

01:07:35.080 --> 01:07:42.840
The qualifying piece is Mozart's Piano Sonata No. 8 in A minor, K?chel 310.

01:07:43.960 --> 01:07:45.473
Your own Mozart?

01:07:46.240 --> 01:07:51.076
I've been telling him to play the piano in his own style, instead of copying others.

01:07:51.720 --> 01:07:54.599
He's already got everything he needs.

01:07:55.120 --> 01:07:56.872
Well that makes it easy!

01:07:58.360 --> 01:08:00.874
You should just play like you play the piano in the forest.

01:08:04.720 --> 01:08:07.109
If that's all I can do, I'll be in trouble.

01:08:08.520 --> 01:08:10.989
She said it would be easy. Damn it...

01:08:21.960 --> 01:08:24.600
What now, you little brat?

01:08:29.840 --> 01:08:31.433
Hey, what's wrong?

01:08:32.960 --> 01:08:33.995
Are you scared?

01:08:36.680 --> 01:08:39.240
I'm not scared. I'm crying because I'm disappointed.

01:08:39.480 --> 01:08:44.111
Because of Amamiya Shuuhei, my plans for winning
the regionals and going to the nationals are—

01:08:45.360 --> 01:08:47.112
Don't blame this on Amamiya!

01:08:48.640 --> 01:08:53.510
| can't believe that Amamiya has to compete against pampered opponents like you!

01:08:53.960 --> 01:08:56.190
He's gonna be the best in Japan!

01:08:56.400 --> 01:09:03.989
It's obvious because he's spent his entire life
enduring painfully tough lessons to get here!

01:09:05.480 --> 01:09:05.992
Have you seen them?

01:09:06.880 --> 01:09:08.154
Have you seen those painful lessons?

01:09:08.640 --> 01:09:11.234
Well, you can't see them.

01:09:12.040 --> 01:09:15.396
Well, what about my lessons? Have you seen my lessons?

01:09:15.880 --> 01:09:18.394
What? How would I have seen them?

01:09:18.920 --> 01:09:22.800
So you have no idea and yet you say such evil things!

01:09:22.800 --> 01:09:23.915
E-Evil?

01:09:26.000 --> 01:09:28.799
I've tried so hard.

01:09:31.680 --> 01:09:33.239
Geez, I've said too much.

01:09:34.560 --> 01:09:37.279
Hey, Takako...

01:09:37.760 --> 01:09:38.670
| don't...

01:09:40.000 --> 01:09:41.798
| don't want to mess up.

01:09:42.640 --> 01:09:44.392
| try not to mess up.

01:09:45.320 --> 01:09:46.549
| play my heart out.

01:09:47.440 --> 01:09:48.032
Always...

01:09:49.040 --> 01:09:50.519
| wear myself out.

01:09:52.560 --> 01:09:56.030
You're not gonna be able to concentrate if you keep thinking such crazy thoughts.

01:09:56.280 --> 01:09:58.669
| know, but I can't help it!

01:09:58.680 --> 01:10:00.273
| guess there's nothing I can do.

01:10:00.960 --> 01:10:03.554
There is one way you can concentrate.

01:10:04.960 --> 01:10:07.952
Think about the place that calms you down the most.

01:10:09.840 --> 01:10:12.912
Imagine it. Imagine that you're in that place.

01:10:15.320 --> 01:10:18.950
The piano's right in front of you. It's just you and the piano.

01:10:22.720 --> 01:10:23.471
The bathroom.

01:10:25.080 --> 01:10:30.200
Oh, geez. We're already running low on time. Go ahead but hurry up.

01:10:31.200 --> 01:10:34.556
No, I mean it's my favorite place, the place that calms me down the most.

01:10:36.360 --> 01:10:37.236
The crapper?

01:10:42.000 --> 01:10:44.992
Elementary

01:10:46.120 --> 01:10:47.110
It's different!

01:10:47.720 --> 01:10:50.758
My bathroom is much bigger and prettier!

01:10:51.320 --> 01:10:53.357
It's completely different from this one!

01:10:54.200 --> 01:10:58.319
Don't be so high and mighty! You're just imagining it, so deal with it!

01:10:58.600 --> 01:11:02.639
My place is a forest, even if there isn't a single tree here!

01:11:04.360 --> 01:11:06.874
| can't do it. I don't have Wendy with me.

01:11:07.240 --> 01:11:08.514
Who's Wendy?

01:11:08.720 --> 01:11:11.633
It's no good unless my dog, Wendy, is by my side!

01:11:11.880 --> 01:11:13.871
A dog?

01:11:15.480 --> 01:11:17.357
You're not gonna find a dog here anywhere!

01:11:17.360 --> 01:11:21.991
| know that, but when I pet her fur while I'm in the bathroom,

01:11:22.240 --> 01:11:24.356
| calm down... I calm down...

01:11:25.880 --> 01:11:28.269
Yeah, I just pet her.

01:11:29.400 --> 01:11:30.674
It's that color, too.

01:11:37.360 --> 01:11:38.634
Wendy!

01:11:40.000 --> 01:11:42.230
No way...

01:11:43.680 --> 01:11:48.629
Would contestants #30 through #37 please begin their preparations backstage?

01:11:49.280 --> 01:11:52.432
Shuuhei-san, you're #31, aren't you?

01:11:53.400 --> 01:11:55.869
Takako-sama!

01:11:56.680 --> 01:12:00.389
What should I do? It's almost time!

01:12:00.880 --> 01:12:03.633
Takako-sama!

01:12:07.840 --> 01:12:09.069
Looks like it's time.

01:12:12.920 --> 01:12:13.716
Can you do this?

01:12:14.080 --> 01:12:15.070
| don't know.

01:12:15.080 --> 01:12:16.070
You can do it!

01:12:24.960 --> 01:12:28.157
| wonder what happened to Kai-kun.

01:12:28.160 --> 01:12:30.470
We're continuing with #31.

01:12:31.080 --> 01:12:33.913
Amamiya Shuuhei-kun will be performing.

01:12:52.600 --> 01:12:53.431
Amamiya-kun.

01:12:53.880 --> 01:12:54.358
Yes, sir.

01:13:10.480 --> 01:13:11.515
Shuuhei-san...

01:13:19.480 --> 01:13:20.754
Oh, God of Piano...

01:13:24.360 --> 01:13:25.111
Please make me...

01:13:27.400 --> 01:13:28.276
number one!

01:14:12.080 --> 01:14:12.956
Yes.

01:14:13.960 --> 01:14:14.711
This is it.

01:14:17.040 --> 01:14:18.439
This is my piano.

01:14:33.960 --> 01:14:35.598
Amamiya's amazing.

01:14:40.800 --> 01:14:42.552
He's so cool.

01:15:23.840 --> 01:15:26.719
| did it. I didn't mess up even once.

01:15:27.880 --> 01:15:28.756
It was flawless.

01:15:29.760 --> 01:15:31.273
Shuuhei-san...

01:15:58.040 --> 01:16:00.316
Kai-kun, I'm sure that...

01:16:01.560 --> 01:16:02.516
| beat you.

01:16:07.160 --> 01:16:13.076
| guess I should have worn long pants like Amamiya
for this competition. Shorts don't really work.

01:16:19.080 --> 01:16:22.835
Amamiya Shuuhei's piano playing was flawless, wasn't it?

01:16:23.440 --> 01:16:25.954
Yeah. But that doesn't matter.

01:16:26.400 --> 01:16:29.438
Takako, just play the best you can.

01:16:30.800 --> 01:16:34.475
| know, Wendy. My opponent is inside of me.

01:16:35.720 --> 01:16:36.710
| know that.

01:16:36.720 --> 01:16:37.710
Wendy... Wendy...

01:16:37.720 --> 01:16:38.676
The next performer is...
Wendy... Wendy...

01:16:38.680 --> 01:16:39.078
The next performer is...

01:16:39.200 --> 01:16:42.591
#33: Maruyama Takako-san.

01:16:44.920 --> 01:16:48.356
Takako, just play like you're in the bathroom with Wendy.

01:17:00.560 --> 01:17:01.880
Young lady...

01:17:11.880 --> 01:17:14.872
Concentrate... Concentrate...

01:17:17.120 --> 01:17:19.999
Wendy, please save me.

01:17:20.400 --> 01:17:23.392
Wendy, please save me. Wendy!

01:17:26.840 --> 01:17:27.830
Wendy...

01:17:44.240 --> 01:17:44.911
Okay!

01:18:27.560 --> 01:18:29.198
Takako-sama!

01:18:44.720 --> 01:18:45.357
I did it.

01:18:48.680 --> 01:18:51.354
They're quite talented this year.

01:19:10.240 --> 01:19:13.358
You did it! You were the perfect "bathroom princess" out there.

01:19:15.360 --> 01:19:16.953
Yup, perfect.

01:19:17.720 --> 01:19:18.516
Thank you.

01:19:19.520 --> 01:19:21.511
You're... You're...

01:19:22.360 --> 01:19:23.839
the best!

01:19:24.480 --> 01:19:25.629
Get off me!

01:19:26.600 --> 01:19:28.273
Sensei, what should I do?

01:19:28.520 --> 01:19:30.238
It's almost Kai's turn.

01:19:30.760 --> 01:19:32.876
My heart is pounding...

01:19:33.400 --> 01:19:38.156
| want to watch him. I really want to watch him, but what if I can't stop my tears?

01:19:38.760 --> 01:19:40.512
If I can't watch him, what should I do?

01:19:41.920 --> 01:19:43.911
You understand, Ichinose.

01:19:45.400 --> 01:19:48.040
Your opponent isn't Mozart.

01:19:49.480 --> 01:19:52.916
You are your own opponent, Ichinose.

01:19:56.040 --> 01:20:00.352
That was #36: Sasaki Maiko-san.

01:20:01.760 --> 01:20:02.431
Kai-kun...

01:20:04.280 --> 01:20:05.873
Performing next is...

01:20:06.160 --> 01:20:09.312
#37: Ichinose Kai-kun.

01:20:11.560 --> 01:20:12.391
Here I go.

01:20:22.080 --> 01:20:22.672
Kai...

01:20:23.320 --> 01:20:25.038
Do your best, Wendy.

01:20:41.560 --> 01:20:42.277
Kai-kun?

01:20:42.840 --> 01:20:44.274
W-Wendy?

01:20:45.720 --> 01:20:46.471
Kai?

01:20:47.960 --> 01:20:50.031
Sh-Shit...

01:20:56.240 --> 01:20:59.790
S-So we meet again, Mozarts.

01:21:09.200 --> 01:21:10.474
Shit!

01:21:12.240 --> 01:21:16.711
Weren't you guys just some ghosts that I originally dreamt up?

01:21:23.960 --> 01:21:26.839
I'll fight through you all...

01:21:31.400 --> 01:21:32.629
until I'm the only one left!

01:21:41.880 --> 01:21:44.110
Kai-kun. Amazing.

01:21:44.520 --> 01:21:46.113
Wendy's so good.

01:21:52.920 --> 01:21:54.399
This kid is skilled.

01:21:55.520 --> 01:21:56.271
Who is he?

01:22:07.280 --> 01:22:08.031
Ichinose...

01:22:09.560 --> 01:22:11.870
Gah, I'm doing it.

01:22:13.640 --> 01:22:19.670
| was so worried about Mozart's ghost, I didn't realize
| was just parroting Ajino's damn playing style.

01:22:20.560 --> 01:22:23.393
Oh, what a shock. It was his final chance, too.

01:22:23.920 --> 01:22:26.799
We're finally gonna get our score back.

01:22:26.800 --> 01:22:28.393
He couldn't do it.

01:22:30.560 --> 01:22:32.631
Give it back, you no-talent kid!

01:22:32.960 --> 01:22:35.952
Give it back!

01:22:35.960 --> 01:22:36.552
Give it back!
Give it back!

01:22:36.560 --> 01:22:37.550
Give it back!

01:22:37.560 --> 01:22:37.913
Give it back!
Give it back!

01:22:37.920 --> 01:22:38.910
Give it back!

01:22:51.960 --> 01:22:52.597
Kai-kun?

01:22:53.960 --> 01:22:54.552
Kai?

01:22:58.440 --> 01:23:01.114
You idiot, Wendy! You can't stop!

01:23:01.480 --> 01:23:04.359
| don't believe it. Why, Kai-kun?

01:23:05.080 --> 01:23:09.119
You didn't mess up once. If you could play like that until the end...

01:23:10.000 --> 01:23:10.717
If you could play...

01:23:16.080 --> 01:23:21.234
I'll give you back the K?chel 310 you're all clamoring for!

01:23:25.360 --> 01:23:26.714
What is he doing?

01:23:29.000 --> 01:23:31.389
I'll play my own K?chel 310—

01:23:43.000 --> 01:23:45.640
Let's go together, to the forest.

01:24:07.800 --> 01:24:08.392
This is it.

01:24:09.640 --> 01:24:10.516
This is the sound.

01:24:12.040 --> 01:24:15.431
What's this? It's not Mozart.

01:24:16.040 --> 01:24:19.032
Sensei, this is the piano in the forest.

01:24:19.040 --> 01:24:19.677
Yes.

01:24:23.920 --> 01:24:27.879
He's playing the piano inside his own world now.

01:24:32.320 --> 01:24:34.960
Most likely, he's made us all into trees.

01:24:35.640 --> 01:24:38.154
And he's turned this hall into the forest.

01:26:14.040 --> 01:26:14.916
I did it.

01:26:37.200 --> 01:26:39.430
Kai was so cool!

01:26:39.920 --> 01:26:41.194
You did it, Wendy!

01:26:41.560 --> 01:26:42.959
Yes, he did it.

01:26:43.520 --> 01:26:44.396
Encore!

01:26:44.400 --> 01:26:44.832
Encore!
Encore!

01:26:44.840 --> 01:26:46.035
Encore!

01:26:46.440 --> 01:26:47.953
Encore!

01:26:57.080 --> 01:26:57.797
I-n

01:26:59.200 --> 01:26:59.837
lost.

01:27:02.080 --> 01:27:05.960
| knew it all along. No matter how hard I tried...

01:27:07.040 --> 01:27:08.439
| was still going to lose.

01:27:09.720 --> 01:27:10.471
In the forest,

01:27:11.720 --> 01:27:12.551
right from the start,

01:27:13.200 --> 01:27:15.111
when I first heard you play the piano,

01:27:19.000 --> 01:27:20.115
| knew it.

01:27:25.880 --> 01:27:28.190
Rei-chan! Ajino!

01:27:29.000 --> 01:27:29.717
Kai!

01:27:30.720 --> 01:27:32.996
| did it! I played my own piano!

01:27:33.880 --> 01:27:36.838
How was it, Ichinose? The best feeling imaginable, right?

01:27:36.840 --> 01:27:38.239
Nope, not at all.

01:27:39.360 --> 01:27:41.874
Don't be so optimistic.

01:27:42.480 --> 01:27:43.629
Wendy!

01:27:45.000 --> 01:27:45.990
Takako!

01:27:49.360 --> 01:27:52.990
Wendy, you were amazing! How did you learn to play the piano like that?

01:27:53.600 --> 01:27:54.749
Wendy?

01:27:54.760 --> 01:27:59.470
At this time, the decisions of the twelve judges will be announced.

01:28:00.240 --> 01:28:07.033
The announcement of the qualifiers will be posted on a display
board in the reception lobby. Please wait a moment.

01:28:14.680 --> 01:28:15.556
Can you see it?

01:28:15.920 --> 01:28:16.273
Yeah.

01:28:16.280 --> 01:28:16.678
Qualifiers (Elementary School Division) Piano
Competition 56th All-Japan Student Yeah.

01:28:16.680 --> 01:28:20.275
Qualifiers (Elementary School Division)
Piano Competition 56th All-Japan Student

01:28:23.760 --> 01:28:24.909
#33...

01:28:24.920 --> 01:28:26.035
#37...

01:28:26.680 --> 01:28:27.909
#33...

01:28:27.920 --> 01:28:29.035
#37...

01:28:32.560 --> 01:28:34.676
#33...

01:28:35.800 --> 01:28:38.553
Amamiya Shuuhei
m100132803381033849328591059049010100

01:28:42.080 --> 01:28:42.273
It's there! It's there!

01:28:42.280 --> 01:28:44.317
It's there! It's there, young lady!
It's there! It's there!

01:28:44.320 --> 01:28:45.435
It's there! It's there, young lady!

01:28:45.440 --> 01:28:45.952
It's there! It's there, young lady!
#37...

01:28:45.960 --> 01:28:46.756
#37...

01:28:47.840 --> 01:28:49.069
#37...

01:28:50.920 --> 01:28:51.557
#37...

01:28:51.560 --> 01:28:52.197
10 names in all
#37...

01:28:52.200 --> 01:28:53.554
10 names in all

01:28:54.960 --> 01:28:55.677
It's not there.

01:28:57.160 --> 01:28:59.197
It's there! It's there!

01:29:00.400 --> 01:29:01.549
Shiraishi!

01:29:04.480 --> 01:29:05.197
Wendy!

01:29:08.680 --> 01:29:11.240
No way. How could they fail you?

01:29:11.680 --> 01:29:13.239
There must have been a mistake.

01:29:13.240 --> 01:29:14.469
Y-Yes!

01:29:14.480 --> 01:29:16.118
That didn't happen.

01:29:16.120 --> 01:29:17.110
But...

01:29:18.120 --> 01:29:19.599
Good luck in the finals.

01:29:21.720 --> 01:29:22.994
Wendy...

01:29:24.000 --> 01:29:25.593
Is that true?

01:29:25.960 --> 01:29:31.876
Yes, though they don't publish the scores, I'm sure you were at the top.

01:29:32.200 --> 01:29:34.953
That's not what I mean. Kai wasn't chosen as a qualifier?

01:29:34.960 --> 01:29:37.349
Well, yes, but that's not that surprising.

01:29:38.240 --> 01:29:41.631
| mean, he just ignored the score and played whatever he felt like.

01:29:44.640 --> 01:29:45.630
Shuuhei-san!

01:29:52.000 --> 01:29:54.514
| felt bad for Ichinose.

01:29:55.640 --> 01:29:58.109
You can't give a ranking to his piano style.

01:29:58.880 --> 01:30:02.635
He doesn't fit within the constructs of the competition.
You can't give him some standard ranking.

01:30:03.160 --> 01:30:06.278
It's unfortunate, but that's the nature of competitions.

01:30:06.720 --> 01:30:08.040
Kai will be fine.

01:30:08.400 --> 01:30:10.152
He'll get over it quickly.

01:30:10.800 --> 01:30:12.791
Kai! You'll catch a cold!

01:30:13.800 --> 01:30:15.120
It feels so good.

01:30:16.120 --> 01:30:19.272
It's going to be a let down after putting so much effort into this.

01:30:20.280 --> 01:30:21.156
Ichinose-san.

01:30:21.400 --> 01:30:21.992
Yes?

01:30:22.920 --> 01:30:23.671
Ichinose...

01:30:24.640 --> 01:30:28.395
No, Kai. May I introduce Kai to the world?

01:30:30.680 --> 01:30:33.559
Japan is too small for his piano.

01:30:35.160 --> 01:30:37.037
So let's show it to the world.

01:30:37.760 --> 01:30:40.513
I'll take him to the rest of the world with me.

01:30:41.560 --> 01:30:42.311
Kai-kun...

01:30:54.400 --> 01:30:55.071
Sensei!

01:30:58.440 --> 01:30:59.316
Where's Kai-kun?

01:30:59.960 --> 01:31:01.598
They just went home.

01:31:01.600 --> 01:31:03.193
I-I see.

01:31:03.200 --> 01:31:08.479
Congratulations on qualifying. You rarely hear such highly accomplished piano playing.

01:31:09.600 --> 01:31:11.830
Th-Thank you very much.

01:31:13.360 --> 01:31:13.952
Sensei!

01:31:15.800 --> 01:31:16.471
Do you think...

01:31:17.080 --> 01:31:23.474
Do you think I could play the piano and move people like
Kai-kun does? Will I be able to play like that someday?

01:31:31.600 --> 01:31:35.594
You need to learn to love your own piano more.

01:31:40.320 --> 01:31:45.713
If you can do that, I'm sure you'll understand. You
won't need to compare yourself to anyone.

01:31:49.360 --> 01:31:50.714
You played the piano well.

01:31:57.760 --> 01:32:02.630
Competition Piano Student
All-dapan Central Region 56th South

01:32:05.120 --> 01:32:09.353
Okay, another big round of applause for Amamiya-kun!

01:32:13.520 --> 01:32:19.914
Now, after that great news, I'm afraid I have to give you some very unfortunate news.

01:32:21.000 --> 01:32:28.555
It's rather sudden, but Amamiya-kun will be going
back to his old elementary school in Tokyo.

01:32:31.280 --> 01:32:32.918
Now it's your turn, Amamiya-kun.

01:32:33.760 --> 01:32:38.755
| was only here for a short time, but I will never forget you all. Thank you very much.

01:32:55.680 --> 01:32:57.557
Well, we'll be going now.

01:32:58.560 --> 01:33:00.710
Shall we go, Shuuhei-san?

01:33:01.280 --> 01:33:03.317
Take care, Amamiya-kun.

01:33:03.320 --> 01:33:03.832
Yes, ma'am.

01:33:17.560 --> 01:33:18.356
Kai-kun...

01:33:20.600 --> 01:33:24.070
Mom, go on ahead. I need to talk to Kai-kun.

01:33:26.840 --> 01:33:29.719
I'm sorry I didn't have the chance to tell you earlier.

01:33:30.920 --> 01:33:35.118
It's fine. Just make sure you win the finals.

01:33:36.480 --> 01:33:40.360
Amamiya, promise me that you'll definitely become the best in Japan.

01:33:42.120 --> 01:33:44.589
If you're not #1, then I'm done with you.

01:33:48.120 --> 01:33:50.839
<i>But you're the true #.</i>

01:33:52.000 --> 01:33:54.230
| actually lost to you.

01:33:55.880 --> 01:33:57.996
Wh-What's wrong, Amamiya?

01:34:00.880 --> 01:34:02.837
Okay, I'll promise you that.

01:34:03.640 --> 01:34:06.154
| can't imagine an opponent better than you.

01:34:07.240 --> 01:34:08.958
Don't say such stupid things!

01:34:08.960 --> 01:34:11.395
Amanmiya, don't underestimate the finals.

01:34:11.400 --> 01:34:14.631
| mean, watch out for the Bathroom Princess! She's a tough opponent.

01:34:15.040 --> 01:34:16.633
Okay, I will.

01:34:18.520 --> 01:34:22.912
I'm gonna be really bored without you.

01:34:24.520 --> 01:34:25.749
Super bored.

01:34:28.160 --> 01:34:28.911
Kai-kun...

01:34:33.560 --> 01:34:36.552
All right, don't forget our promise! The best in Japan!

01:34:39.800 --> 01:34:44.556
You'd better! Because I'm always going to brag about you!

01:34:47.200 --> 01:34:48.270
Kai-kun!

01:34:49.000 --> 01:34:52.550
Amamiya, do your best. Do your best! Do your best!

01:34:58.920 --> 01:34:59.512
Kai-kun...

01:35:00.920 --> 01:35:01.637
Thank you.

01:35:12.600 --> 01:35:17.436
If I had never met you,

01:35:19.080 --> 01:35:22.198
I'm sure I would have ended up hating the piano.

01:35:23.920 --> 01:35:25.593
Oh, the forest...

01:36:32.920 --> 01:36:40.920
Please stay by my side as I'm about to fall asleep
onegai soba ni ite yo sugu ni nemuru kara

01:36:44.160 --> 01:36:52.160
The moonlit night that's made its way to my window
tsuki no kagayaku yoru ga madobe made kiteru

01:36:54.440 --> 01:37:02.440
has unfastened the lock to my heart
kokoro ni kaketeta kagi no hazushita

01:37:08.160 --> 01:37:16.160
Since someday even my grief will be transformed into memories
itami sae mo itsuka wa omoide e to kawaru kara

01:37:18.960 --> 01:37:26.960
| want to sleep, enjoying sweet dreams, until the morning comes
yasashii yume wo minagara nemuritai asa ga kuru made

01:37:46.200 --> 01:37:54.200
I've had happy nights, and sleepless nights too
shiawasena yoru ga aru nemurenai yoru mo

01:37:57.360 --> 01:38:05.360
You know you've given both of those to me
sono dochira mo anata ga watashi ni kureta ne

01:38:07.840 --> 01:38:15.840
Tomorrow I'll be leaving the forest as well
ashita wa watashi mo mori wo dete yuku

01:38:21.640 --> 01:38:29.640
Though I don't know where my feelings have run off to
hashiridashita omoi no yukisaki wa shiranai kedo

01:38:32.480 --> 01:38:40.480
I'll keep on believing and press on to where the light is shining over you
hikari no terasu ga anata e susundeku shinjiru mama ni

01:38:50.520 --> 01:38:58.520
When I nestle my face against you, you seem to melt
hoozuri shitara tokechaisonna yokogao

01:39:01.800 --> 01:39:09.800
Even so, I want to be next to you forever
tonari ni zutto itai kedo

01:39:12.560 --> 01:39:20.560
I'll never forget the time we spent passing through the forest of dreams
yume no mori ga sugoshita toki wo kitto wasurenai

01:39:23.600 --> 01:39:31.600
This is not our final goodbye
saigo no wakare ja nai yo

01:39:34.800 --> 01:39:42.800
Thank you for all the tender days
arigatou yawarakana hibi

01:39:46.240 --> 01:39:49.240
Farewell, until we meet again
sayounara mata au hi made
